// resources.rc.in — carries Sunshine inside the executable.
//
// SolStream ships as one file. Sunshine is 65 MB of unmodified upstream binary
// that has to end up beside the program, and a folder of loose files is not
// something a person downloads and runs: they unzip it to Downloads, run the
// exe out of there, and the install works but lives somewhere temporary.
//
// So the archive is a resource. `--install` writes it out and unpacks it into
// Program Files, after which the executable and its Sunshine sit together the
// way the rest of the program already expects. Nothing about the runtime layout
// changes; only how it arrives.
//
// Configured by CMake, which substitutes the path to the archive it was told to
// embed. Backslashes are doubled because RC treats them as escapes.

SUNSHINE_ARCHIVE RCDATA "@SOLSTREAM_SUNSHINE_ZIP_RC@"
